    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "idk. i just don't see the beauty in it. it just feels like a lot of noise. if a program is buggy and just creates errors without serving a purpose, the standard protocol is to terminate it. why should humans be any different? it feels like staying alive is just staying in a loop of errors.",
